From 17ab74e7357a3d10d4ce516f94ececa10a91d38f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nathan Safran <nsafran1217@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:21:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 542/634] IA64: fix inverted
 ptrace_report_syscall_permit_entry() check

7.3 replaced ptrace_report_syscall_entry() (nonzero = abort the syscall)
with ptrace_report_syscall_permit_entry() (true = let the syscall run).
The ia64 port was converted by renaming the call only, so any traced
syscall that the tracer allows is aborted with -ENOSYS.  Symptom: under
strace every syscall fails, e.g. `strace /bin/true` shows
execve(...) = -1 ENOSYS and the child dies with SIGILL.  Every other
architecture tests !ptrace_report_syscall_permit_entry().

Fixes: 0473c96179527ec338b0d0d950b31090921a6b83 ("ia64: Replace ptrace_report_syscall_entry() call with ptrace_report_syscall_permit_entry()")
Signed-off-by: Nathan Safran <nsafran1217@gmail.com>
---
 arch/ia64/kernel/ptrace.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/ia64/kernel/ptrace.c b/arch/ia64/kernel/ptrace.c
index 544e9f8051ac8..98c0b0b88a488 100644
--- a/arch/ia64/kernel/ptrace.c
+++ b/arch/ia64/kernel/ptrace.c
@@ -1173,7 +1173,7 @@ syscall_trace_enter (long arg0, long arg1, long arg2, long arg3,
 		     struct pt_regs regs)
 {
 	if (test_thread_flag(TIF_SYSCALL_TRACE))
-		if (ptrace_report_syscall_permit_entry(&regs))
+		if (!ptrace_report_syscall_permit_entry(&regs))
 			return -ENOSYS;
 
 	/* copy user rbs to kernel rbs */
